  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How does a suspension bridge work?",
      "a": "The deck hangs from vertical hangers attached to main cables. The cables run over tall towers and are anchored at both ends, so the load is carried in tension by the cables and in compression by the towers.",
      "asks": [
        "What is a suspension bridge?",
        "How do suspension bridges stay up?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What are the hangers on a suspension bridge?",
      "a": "Hangers, also called suspenders, are the vertical steel ropes that connect the deck to the main cables. Each one carries a short length of the deck.",
      "asks": [
        "What are the vertical cables on a bridge?",
        "What are suspenders?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do suspension bridges have tall towers?",
      "a": "The towers hold the main cables high so they can sag in a curve across the span. They take the downward push of the cables and press it into their foundations.",
      "asks": [
        "What do the towers do?",
        "Why are the towers so tall?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is an anchorage?",
      "a": "An anchorage is the giant block of concrete, or a tunnel into rock, where each main cable is tied down at the ends of the bridge. It resists the cables' enormous pull.",
      "asks": [
        "What holds the ends of the cables?",
        "Where are suspension bridge cables attached?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the longest suspension bridge?",
      "a": "The 1915 Çanakkale Bridge in Turkey, opened in 2022, has the longest main span of any suspension bridge: 2,023 metres between its towers.",
      "asks": [
        "Which bridge has the longest span?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    "The 1915 Çanakkale Bridge in Turkey, opened in 2022, has a main span of 2,023 metres, the longest of any suspension bridge.",
